## Why This Is Asked
This question probes cross-region consistency, conflict resolution, and practical MongoDB usage.

## Key Concepts
- CAP trade-offs in distributed systems
- Per-field versioning and conflict resolution
- ReadConcern/WriteConcern in MongoDB

## Code Example
```javascript
function mergePrefs(existing, incoming) {
  const out = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(existing || {}));
  for (const key of Object.keys(incoming)) {
    const inc = incoming[key];
    const cur = out[key];
    const tsInc = inc.__version?.ts ?? 0;
    const tsCur = cur?.__version?.ts ?? -1;
    if (tsInc > tsCur || (tsInc === tsCur && (inc.__version?.clientId ?? 0) < (cur?.__version?.clientId ?? 0))) {
      out[key] = inc;
    }
  }
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this merge under simultaneous updates?
- How would you adapt for field-level strong consistency needs?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests integration of privacy-preserving computation with hardware-assisted trust, and designs that scale across untrusted fog nodes while preserving tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Threshold cryptography
- Trusted Execution Environments
- Secure aggregation
- Provenance and replay protection
- Cross-tenant isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal handler sketch for /cca_score/tt_share
async function handleShare(req){
  const {tenant_id, device_id, t_of_n, shard, attestation, nonce} = req.body;
  if(!verifyAttestation(attestation, device_id)) throw new Error("Bad attestation");
  // store share and nonce for later aggregation
  await storeShare(tenant_id, device_id, t_of_n, shard, nonce);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle stragglers and missing shares in the t-of-n scheme?
- What are the security trade-offs of using TEEs vs. pure MPC for this use case?

